#!/usr/bin/env python3
# section: 1
"""hee-exif: real EXIF read + a real, doctrine-grounded signature write
for any photo TCOS serves publicly.

Real trigger (2026-08-25, Spencer): "make sure we have all exif we can
get in exif on all photos we serve" + "need to settle on our sig" --
while publishing the first real spencer.media.lab.tcos.us photo
gallery and finding that Google Photos' own album-level date range was
actively misleading (a real single-session tattoo mis-read as spanning
years) until each photo's own real EXIF DateTimeOriginal corrected it.

Signature design is NOT invented here. contracts/agent-instance-
signature-v1.contract.yaml already defines the real signature-block
this org uses for messages/comments and explicitly says: "if a
stronger identifier is ever needed, extend this contract's
signature-block rather than starting a third parallel identity
scheme." Confirmed with Spencer (2026-08-25): reuse those same 4
fields (session_id, host, gh_actor, timestamp) verbatim, sourced the
same way tools/agent-signature.sh sources them -- don't reimplement
that sourcing logic, shell out to the real script.

Requires exiftool (libimage-exiftool-perl) -- the only tool here
robust enough to both read everything a JPEG can carry and write
custom fields without clobbering real original data (DateTimeOriginal,
Model, any pre-existing Artist/Copyright, embedded Photoshop history,
etc). Never touches those; only ever ADDS to UserComment and sets
Artist/Copyright when explicitly given AND not already present.

Usage:
  hee-exif read <file-or-url> [--json]
  hee-exif verify <file-or-url>... [--pixels OURS]
      --pixels OURS compares each file's decoded pixels, frame by frame,
      against OURS (a file or URL we hold, ideally signed): identical
      pixels, frame count and timing -> OK; same size and frames with a
      mean per-channel difference under 2/255 -> WARNING "re-encoded"
      (a lossy platform copy); anything else -> CRITICAL, naming the first
      differing frame. This is a claim RELATIVE TO OUR COPY, not a
      signature in theirs -- the honest statement for a platform repost.
      Measured 2026-09-05 on a Discord repost of the MN2600 GIF: Discord
      strips every XMP block and rewrites the container, so no signature
      survives, but the pixels do (human-execution-engine#557).
      Both accept a URL wherever a file is expected: anything curl can
      fetch -- https, http, gopher, ftp, file. The body is fetched to a
      temp file (the URL's own filename extension kept, so exiftool sees
      the same container) and read from there; nothing is written back.
      Operator, 2026-09-05: "make hee exif read urls too (any type of url
      where an image might be, including gopher)" -- the real use is a
      copy of our image that someone reposted: verify says whether the
      embedded signature survived the trip.
  hee-exif brand <file>... [--branding FILE] [--artist NAME] [--copyright TEXT]
                        [--force] [--dry-run]
      The org's default branding, from one YAML card (tcos-audit's
      policy/branding.card.v1.yaml; path via --branding or $HEE_BRANDING,
      set in heerc). Always written: Credit + Publisher = the org's long
      name (the publisher line "will always be our long name" --
      operator, 2026-09-05), the PEN as an identifier (urn:oid:1.3.6.1.4.1.<pen>),
      and the license (UsageTerms, WebStatement, Marked). Defaulted
      unless given: Artist = the org's long name, Copyright = the org's
      notice with this year. --artist/--copyright name someone else when
      the work is THEIR IP and we are only sharing it (operator, same
      day) -- precedent: spencer.media.tcos.us/tux-tattoo, where Artist
      and Copyright are the tattoo artist's. Existing real Artist /
      Copyright values are left alone unless --force, same rule as sign.
  hee-exif embed-sig <file>... [--key GPG-KEY-ID] [--dry-run]
      Put a GPG signature IN the file. Signs the file's metadata-stripped
      form (`exiftool -all=`, deterministic per container -- measured on
      JPEG, PNG, GIF) and writes the armored signature, the signer's
      fingerprint, the signed sha256 and the recipe into the TCOS XMP
      namespace (XMP-hee:*, library/exiftool/hee-xmp.config). Stays valid
      through every later metadata write, because none of that is in the
      signed form. Operator, 2026-09-05: "can we put the gpg sig in the
      exif?" -- yes, this way: a detached .asc stays on our page, this
      one travels with the file wherever it is reposted.
  hee-exif verify <file>...
      Check an embedded signature: strip the same way, gpg --verify the
      embedded armor against it, compare the digest. Also checks a
      detached <file>.asc beside it (gpg-sign's, over the served bytes)
      when present. Nagios exit codes: 0 OK, 2 CRITICAL (any bad or
      missing), 3 UNKNOWN (no exiftool/gpg).
  hee-exif provenance <file>... --tool NAME [--commit SHA] [--job PATH]
                        [--source PATH] [--kv k=v]... [--force] [--dry-run]
      How a GENERATED image came to be -- the deterministic-flow
      counterpart of `sign`. Writes XMP-xmp:CreatorTool (tool@commit),
      XMP-dc:Source (the input file + its sha256) and XMP-dc:Description
      ("provenance: tool=..; commit=..; job=..; job_sha256=..;
      source_sha256=..; k=v..; signed=<sig_tag>"), mirrored to
      EXIF:ImageDescription / IPTC:Caption-Abstract on JPEG. The
      signature is the org's sig_tag form (host-user-<hash>_<tmux>), read
      from hee-ver session, never invented. An existing Description that
      is not a provenance block is left alone unless --force. Works on
      JPEG, PNG and GIF (XMP travels in all three; measured 2026-09-05).
      Real trigger: fleet-ops#381 review, "how can we introduce ... our
      exif tools to this" -- meme-factory renders from a job file with
      no agent in the loop, so `sign`'s session fields are `unknown` by
      construction; what such an output can truthfully carry is which
      tool, which commit, which job and which source made it.
      Paths are recorded RELATIVE, never absolute (operator, 2026-09-05:
      "do not want full local paths"): a path inside a git checkout is
      recorded as <repo-dir-name>/<path-from-repo-root>; anything else is
      recorded relative to the stamped file's own directory. The sha256
      is always of the real file.
  hee-exif sign <file> [--artist NAME] [--copyright TEXT]
                        [--force] [--dry-run]
      --force overwrites an already-set Artist/Copyright; without it,
      an existing real value is left alone and reported, never guessed
      over. Artist/Copyright are mirrored into IPTC/XMP equivalents
      too (IPTC:By-line/XMP:Creator/XMP:ImageCreatorName for Artist;
      IPTC:CopyrightNotice/XMP:Rights for Copyright) -- real prior art
      from Spencer's own 2020 exif-update.sh, since different
      platforms only read one of the three metadata standards for the
      same real-world fact.
  hee-exif regen-pubkey <target-html> <var-name> <github-login>
      Front-loads a GPG public key from the real canonical source
      (github.com/<login>.gpg) into a `var <var-name> = "...";` JS
      constant in target-html. Real trigger (2026-08-26, Spencer):
      "front load that var from gh/oper.gpg instead" of hand-copying a
      key once -- covers a future key rotation with a re-run, not
      another manual copy-paste. Has to embed at generation time, not
      fetch client-side: github.com/*.gpg has no CORS headers,
      confirmed live.
  hee-exif embed-exif <target-html> <var-name> <photo-dir>
                       [--exclude field1,field2,...]
      Embeds real, complete (non-blank) exiftool output for every
      .jpg/.jpeg in photo-dir into a `var <var-name> = {...};` JS
      constant in target-html, keyed by filename (no extension).
      --exclude defaults to fields tied to the *local copy* used for
      extraction, not the real photo (paths, local access/modify/inode
      timestamps, permissions) -- override if a target has different
      needs.
"""
import argparse
import json
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import urllib.request
from pathlib import Path

# library/py lives in this tool's own repo -- derive it from this script's
# own location, resolved through symlinks, never from the repo the tool
# happens to be invoked against.
from pathlib import Path as _Path  # noqa: E402
sys.path.insert(0, str(_Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent / "library" / "py"))
from hee_cli import help_wanted, note_ignored  # noqa: E402

REPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
AGENT_SIG = REPO_ROOT / "tools" / "agent-signature.sh"

# Real, confirmed legal name (Spencer, 2026-08-25) -- the registered
# MN entity name, not the domain. Deliberately NOT auto-applied as a
# --copyright default (real mistake, caught the same day): copyright
# vests in whoever actually created the work (17 U.S.C. Sec 102) --
# writing this org's name onto a photo someone else took is a false
# legal claim, not a formatting choice. --copyright must be passed
# explicitly, only when real authorship/assignment is actually known.
TCOS_LEGAL_NAME = "Twin Cities Open Systems - Operations LLC"


def run(cmd, **kw):
    return subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, **kw)


def require_exiftool():
    if run(["which", "exiftool"]).returncode != 0:
        sys.exit("hee-exif: exiftool not found -- install libimage-exiftool-perl")


URL_SCHEMES = ("http://", "https://", "gopher://", "ftp://", "file://")


def fetch_if_url(path, tmpdir):
    """A URL becomes a local temp file (curl, so gopher/ftp/file work too);
    a path is returned as-is. The URL's own filename extension is kept so
    exiftool sees the same container it would on disk."""
    if not str(path).startswith(URL_SCHEMES):
        return path
    from urllib.parse import urlparse
    name = Path(urlparse(path).path).name or "download"
    out = Path(tmpdir) / name
    r = run(["curl", "-sSL", "--fail", "--max-time", "60", "-o", str(out), path])
    if r.returncode != 0 or not out.is_file():
        sys.exit(f"hee-exif: fetch failed for {path}: {r.stderr.strip()}")
    print(f"hee-exif: fetched {path} -> {out.stat().st_size} bytes", file=sys.stderr)
    return str(out)


def cmd_read(args):
    import tempfile
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as _td:
        args.file = fetch_if_url(args.file, _td)
        return _cmd_read(args)


def _cmd_read(args):
    require_exiftool()
    fmt = ["-j"] if args.json else ["-a", "-G1"]
    proc = run(["exiftool", *fmt, args.file])
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        sys.exit(f"hee-exif: exiftool failed:\n{proc.stderr}")
    if args.json:
        print(json.dumps(json.loads(proc.stdout)[0], indent=2))
    else:
        print(proc.stdout)


def get_agent_signature_fields():
    """Real fields only, sourced via tools/agent-signature.sh -- not
    reimplemented here, so there is exactly one place that knows how
    to read session_id/host/gh_actor/timestamp from this environment."""
    if not AGENT_SIG.exists():
        sys.exit(f"hee-exif: {AGENT_SIG} not found -- can't source signature fields")
    proc = run(["bash", str(AGENT_SIG)])
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        sys.exit(f"hee-exif: agent-signature.sh failed:\n{proc.stderr}")
    wanted = {"session_id", "host", "gh_actor", "timestamp"}
    fields = {}
    for line in proc.stdout.splitlines():
        if ":" not in line:
            continue
        k, v = line.split(":", 1)
        k = k.strip()
        if k in wanted:
            fields[k] = v.strip()
    missing = wanted - fields.keys()
    if missing:
        sys.exit(f"hee-exif: agent-signature.sh didn't report expected fields: {missing}")
    return fields


def existing_tag(file, tag):
    proc = run(["exiftool", f"-{tag}", "-s3", file])
    val = proc.stdout.strip()
    return val or None


def cmd_sign(args):
    require_exiftool()
    fields = get_agent_signature_fields()
    comment = "; ".join(f"{k}={v}" for k, v in fields.items())

    exif_args = ["exiftool", "-overwrite_original"]
    report = []

    exif_args.append(f"-UserComment={comment}")
    report.append(f"UserComment: {comment}")

    # Real prior art, found live 2026-08-26 (Spencer's own 2020
    # exif-update.sh): different platforms/tools read different
    # metadata standards for the same real-world fact -- some only
    # check legacy EXIF, others only IPTC or XMP. Mirroring
    # Artist/Copyright across all three is what actually makes
    # attribution show up everywhere, not just in exiftool's own dump.
    # Gate stays on the primary EXIF tag's existing value, same
    # never-guess-over-a-real-value rule as before -- if that one's
    # already set, none of its mirrors get touched either.
    MIRROR_TAGS = {
        "Artist": ["IPTC:By-line", "XMP:Creator", "XMP:ImageCreatorName"],
        "Copyright": ["IPTC:CopyrightNotice", "XMP:Rights"],
    }
    for tag, value in (("Artist", args.artist), ("Copyright", args.copyright)):
        if value is None:
            continue
        current = existing_tag(args.file, tag)
        if current and not args.force:
            report.append(f"{tag}: SKIPPED (already set to {current!r}; use --force to overwrite)")
            continue
        exif_args.append(f"-{tag}={value}")
        report.append(f"{tag}: {value}" + (" (overwriting real existing value!)" if current else ""))
        for mirror in MIRROR_TAGS[tag]:
            exif_args.append(f"-{mirror}={value}")
            report.append(f"{mirror}: {value}")

    if args.dry_run:
        print("hee-exif sign --dry-run, would write:")
        for line in report:
            print(f"  {line}")
        return

    exif_args.append(args.file)
    proc = run(exif_args)
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        sys.exit(f"hee-exif: exiftool write failed:\n{proc.stderr}")
    for line in report:
        print(line)
    print(f"hee-exif: wrote signature to {args.file}")


def sha256_of(path):
    import hashlib
    h = hashlib.sha256()
    with open(path, "rb") as fh:
        for chunk in iter(lambda: fh.read(1 << 20), b""):
            h.update(chunk)
    return h.hexdigest()


def sig_tag():
    """The org's instance signature in sig_tag form, from hee-ver session --
    the same source every other signer uses. Falls back to host-user when
    hee-ver is unavailable, and says so rather than inventing a hash."""
    ver = Path(__file__).resolve().parent / "hee-ver"
    try:
        out = json.loads(run([str(ver), "session", "--json"]).stdout)
        tag = out.get("session", out).get("sig_tag")
        if tag:
            return tag
    except Exception:
        pass
    import getpass, socket
    return f"{socket.gethostname().split('.')[0]}-{getpass.getuser()}-nosession"


def relative_label(path, anchor_file):
    """A path for the record: never absolute. Inside a git checkout ->
    '<repo dir name>/<path from repo root>'; otherwise relative to the
    stamped file's directory, falling back to the basename."""
    p = Path(path).resolve()
    r = run(["git", "-C", str(p.parent if p.is_file() else p), "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"])
    if r.returncode == 0 and r.stdout.strip():
        top = Path(r.stdout.strip())
        try:
            return f"{top.name}/{p.relative_to(top)}"
        except ValueError:
            pass
    try:
        import os
        rel = os.path.relpath(p, Path(anchor_file).resolve().parent)
    except ValueError:
        return p.name
    # "../../../../mnt/..." is not a relative label, it is an absolute path
    # in disguise (measured 2026-09-05 when outputs were redirected to a
    # scratch dir while the source stayed on the share). Beside or below
    # the stamped file: keep the path. Anywhere else: just the name.
    return p.name if rel.startswith("..") else rel


def load_branding(path):
    try:
        import yaml
    except ImportError:
        sys.exit("hee-exif brand: needs pyyaml (python3-yaml)")
    if not path:
        sys.exit("hee-exif brand: no branding file -- pass --branding FILE or set HEE_BRANDING (heerc) "
                 "to tcos-audit/policy/branding.card.v1.yaml")
    if not Path(path).is_file():
        sys.exit(f"hee-exif brand: branding file not found: {path}")
    d = yaml.safe_load(Path(path).read_text())
    if d.get("kind") != "Card" or d.get("apiVersion") != "hee/v1":
        sys.exit(f"hee-exif brand: {path} is not an apiVersion hee/v1 kind Card")
    return d["spec"]


def cmd_brand(args):
    import datetime, os
    require_exiftool()
    spec = load_branding(args.branding or os.environ.get("HEE_BRANDING"))
    name_full = spec["name"]["full"]
    publisher = spec.get("credit", {}).get("publisher", name_full)
    year = str(datetime.date.today().year)
    artist = args.artist or name_full
    copyright_ = args.copyright or spec["copyright"]["notice"].replace("{year}", year)
    lic = spec.get("license", {})
    urn = spec.get("identifier", {}).get("urn")
    # Always-on org fields. Credit/Publisher name the publisher, even when
    # Artist/Copyright below name someone else because the work is theirs.
    always = [
        ("IPTC:Credit", publisher), ("XMP-photoshop:Credit", publisher), ("XMP-dc:Publisher", publisher),
        ("XMP-xmpRights:Marked", "True"),
    ]
    if lic.get("url"):
        always.append(("XMP-xmpRights:WebStatement", lic["url"]))
    if lic.get("name"):
        always.append(("XMP-xmpRights:UsageTerms", f"{lic['name']} ({lic.get('spdx', '')}) -- {lic.get('url', '')}".strip()))
    if urn:
        always += [("XMP-xmp:Identifier", urn), ("XMP-dc:Identifier", urn)]
    # JPEG-only groups get filtered per container, same reason as provenance.
    MIRROR = {"Artist": ["IPTC:By-line", "XMP:Creator", "XMP:ImageCreatorName"],
              "Copyright": ["IPTC:CopyrightNotice", "XMP:Rights"]}
    rc = 0
    for file in args.files:
        jpeg = Path(file).suffix.lower() in (".jpg", ".jpeg")
        exif_args = ["exiftool", "-overwrite_original"]
        report = []
        for tag, value in always:
            if not jpeg and tag.startswith("IPTC:"):
                continue
            exif_args.append(f"-{tag}={value}"); report.append(f"{tag}: {value}")
        for tag, value in (("Artist", artist), ("Copyright", copyright_)):
            current = existing_tag(file, tag) if jpeg else existing_tag(file, MIRROR[tag][1])
            if current and not args.force:
                report.append(f"{tag}: SKIPPED (already set to {current!r}; use --force)")
                continue
            if jpeg:
                exif_args.append(f"-{tag}={value}")
            report.append(f"{tag}: {value}")
            for mirror in MIRROR[tag]:
                if not jpeg and mirror.startswith("IPTC:"):
                    continue
                exif_args.append(f"-{mirror}={value}")
        if args.dry_run:
            print(f"hee-exif brand --dry-run, would write to {file}:")
            for line in report:
                print(f"  {line}")
            continue
        r = run(exif_args + [file])
        if r.returncode != 0:
            print(f"hee-exif brand: FAILED on {file}: {r.stderr.strip()}", file=sys.stderr); rc = 2; continue
        print(f"hee-exif brand: {file}")
        for line in report:
            print(f"  {line}")
    return rc


XMP_CONFIG = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent / "library" / "exiftool" / "hee-xmp.config"
SIGNED_FORM = "exiftool -all="


def stripped_form(file, tmpdir):
    """The bytes that get signed: the file with every metadata block removed,
    written by exiftool -- the same command at sign and verify time."""
    out = Path(tmpdir) / ("stripped" + Path(file).suffix)
    r = run(["exiftool", "-all=", "-o", str(out), str(file)])
    if r.returncode != 0 or not out.is_file():
        sys.exit(f"hee-exif: could not produce the stripped form of {file}: {r.stderr.strip()}")
    return out


def gpg_fingerprint(key):
    r = run(["gpg", "--list-secret-keys", "--with-colons"] + ([key] if key else []))
    for line in r.stdout.splitlines():
        if line.startswith("fpr:"):
            return line.split(":")[9]
    return None


def cmd_embed_sig(args):
    import tempfile
    require_exiftool()
    if run(["which", "gpg"]).returncode != 0:
        sys.exit("hee-exif embed-sig: gpg not found")
    fpr = gpg_fingerprint(args.key)
    if not fpr:
        sys.exit(f"hee-exif embed-sig: no secret key{' for ' + args.key if args.key else ''}")
    rc = 0
    for file in args.files:
        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as td:
            form = stripped_form(file, td)
            digest = sha256_of(form)
            cmd = ["gpg", "--batch", "--yes", "--detach-sign", "--armor", "--output", "-"] + (["--local-user", args.key] if args.key else []) + [str(form)]
            if args.dry_run:
                print(f"hee-exif embed-sig --dry-run: {file}\n  signed form sha256 {digest} by {fpr}\n  would run: {' '.join(cmd)}")
                continue
            r = run(cmd)
            if r.returncode != 0:
                print(f"hee-exif embed-sig: gpg FAILED on {file}: {r.stderr.strip()}", file=sys.stderr); rc = 2; continue
            armored = r.stdout
            w = run(["exiftool", "-config", str(XMP_CONFIG), "-overwrite_original",
                     f"-XMP-hee:LabSignature={armored}", f"-XMP-hee:LabSigner={fpr}",
                     f"-XMP-hee:SignedDigest={digest}", f"-XMP-hee:SignedForm={SIGNED_FORM}", str(file)])
            if w.returncode != 0:
                print(f"hee-exif embed-sig: exiftool FAILED on {file}: {w.stderr.strip()}", file=sys.stderr); rc = 2; continue
            print(f"hee-exif embed-sig: {file}\n  XMP-hee:LabSigner: {fpr}\n  XMP-hee:SignedDigest: {digest}\n  XMP-hee:SignedForm: {SIGNED_FORM}")
    return rc


def pixel_compare(theirs, ours):
    """Frame-by-frame pixel comparison, pure Pillow (no numpy on the host
    python). Returns (status, message) with status 0/1/2. Any decode
    failure -- truncated data surfaces only when a frame is converted --
    is a CRITICAL report, never an exception."""
    try:
        return _pixel_compare(theirs, ours)
    except Exception as e:
        return 2, f"cannot decode: {e}"


def _pixel_compare(theirs, ours):
    from PIL import Image, ImageChops, ImageSequence, ImageStat
    a, b = Image.open(theirs), Image.open(ours)
    na, nb = getattr(a, "n_frames", 1), getattr(b, "n_frames", 1)
    if a.size != b.size:
        return 2, f"size differs: theirs {a.size[0]}x{a.size[1]}, ours {b.size[0]}x{b.size[1]}"
    if na != nb:
        return 2, f"frame count differs: theirs {na}, ours {nb}"
    worst_mean, first_diff, timing_diff = 0.0, None, None
    for i, (fa, fb) in enumerate(zip(ImageSequence.Iterator(a), ImageSequence.Iterator(b))):
        da, db = fa.info.get("duration"), fb.info.get("duration")
        if da != db and timing_diff is None:
            timing_diff = (i, da, db)
        diff = ImageChops.difference(fa.convert("RGB"), fb.convert("RGB"))
        if diff.getbbox() is None:
            continue
        mean = sum(ImageStat.Stat(diff).mean) / 3.0
        worst_mean = max(worst_mean, mean)
        if first_diff is None:
            first_diff = (i, mean)
    if first_diff is None and timing_diff is None:
        return 0, f"pixels identical to ours, {na} frame(s), timing identical"
    if first_diff is None:
        i, da, db = timing_diff
        return 1, f"pixels identical, but frame {i} timing differs (theirs {da} ms, ours {db} ms)"
    if worst_mean < 2.0:
        return 1, f"re-encoded: same size and {na} frame(s), pixels differ by a mean of {worst_mean:.2f}/255 at worst (first at frame {first_diff[0]})"
    return 2, f"pixels differ: mean {worst_mean:.1f}/255 at worst, first at frame {first_diff[0]}"


def cmd_verify(args):
    import tempfile
    require_exiftool()
    if run(["which", "gpg"]).returncode != 0:
        print("⚠️ UNKNOWN hee-exif verify: gpg not found"); return 3
    worst = 0
    _fetch_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp()
    ours = fetch_if_url(args.pixels, _fetch_dir) if args.pixels else None
    for file in args.files:
        label = file
        file = fetch_if_url(file, _fetch_dir)
        if ours:
            st, msg = pixel_compare(file, ours)
            print(f"{['✅ OK      ', '⚠️ WARNING ', '❌ CRITICAL'][st]} {label}: {msg}")
            worst = max(worst, st)
            if args.pixels_only:
                continue
        r = run(["exiftool", "-config", str(XMP_CONFIG), "-b", "-XMP-hee:LabSignature", str(file)])
        armored = r.stdout
        digest_claim = run(["exiftool", "-config", str(XMP_CONFIG), "-s3", "-XMP-hee:SignedDigest", str(file)]).stdout.strip()
        if "BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE" not in armored:
            print(f"❌ CRITICAL {label}: no embedded signature (XMP-hee:LabSignature)"); worst = max(worst, 2)
        else:
            with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as td:
                form = stripped_form(file, td)
                digest = sha256_of(form)
                sig = Path(td) / "embedded.asc"; sig.write_text(armored if armored.endswith("\n") else armored + "\n")
                v = run(["gpg", "--batch", "--verify", str(sig), str(form)])
                good = v.returncode == 0
                who = next((l for l in v.stderr.splitlines() if "Good signature" in l or "BAD signature" in l), v.stderr.strip().splitlines()[-1] if v.stderr.strip() else "")
                if good and digest == digest_claim:
                    print(f"✅ OK       {label}: embedded signature verifies over the stripped form -- {who.strip()}")
                else:
                    print(f"❌ CRITICAL {label}: embedded signature {'verifies but digest claim differs' if good else 'does NOT verify'} -- {who.strip()}"); worst = max(worst, 2)
        asc = Path(str(file) + ".asc")
        if asc.is_file():
            v = run(["gpg", "--batch", "--verify", str(asc), str(file)])
            if v.returncode == 0:
                print(f"✅ OK       {label}: detached {asc.name} verifies over the served bytes")
            else:
                print(f"❌ CRITICAL {label}: detached {asc.name} does NOT verify (file changed after signing?)"); worst = max(worst, 2)
    return worst


def cmd_provenance(args):
    require_exiftool()
    kv = []
    kv.append(("tool", args.tool))
    if args.commit:
        kv.append(("commit", args.commit))
    anchor_file = args.files[0]
    if args.job:
        kv.append(("job", relative_label(args.job, anchor_file)))
        if Path(args.job).is_file():
            kv.append(("job_sha256", sha256_of(args.job)))
    src_desc = None
    if args.source:
        src_label = relative_label(args.source, anchor_file)
        kv.append(("source", src_label))
        if Path(args.source).is_file():
            h = sha256_of(args.source)
            kv.append(("source_sha256", h))
            src_desc = f"{src_label} sha256:{h}"
        else:
            src_desc = src_label
    for item in args.kv or []:
        if "=" not in item:
            sys.exit(f"hee-exif provenance: --kv wants k=v, got {item!r}")
        k, v = item.split("=", 1)
        kv.append((k, v))
    kv.append(("signed", sig_tag()))
    desc = "provenance: " + "; ".join(f"{k}={v}" for k, v in kv)
    creator = args.tool + (f"@{args.commit}" if args.commit else "")

    rc = 0
    for file in args.files:
        report = []
        exif_args = ["exiftool", "-overwrite_original", f"-XMP-xmp:CreatorTool={creator}"]
        report.append(f"XMP-xmp:CreatorTool: {creator}")
        if src_desc:
            exif_args.append(f"-XMP-dc:Source={src_desc}")
            report.append(f"XMP-dc:Source: {src_desc}")
        current = existing_tag(file, "XMP-dc:Description")
        if current and not current.startswith("provenance:") and not args.force:
            report.append(f"XMP-dc:Description: SKIPPED (already set to {current!r}, not a provenance block; use --force)")
        else:
            exif_args.append(f"-XMP-dc:Description={desc}")
            report.append(f"XMP-dc:Description: {desc}")
            # Same mirroring rule as Artist/Copyright in `sign`: platforms
            # read different standards for the same fact. EXIF and IPTC
            # only exist in JPEG; writing them to PNG/GIF makes exiftool
            # refuse the whole command, so gate on the container.
            if Path(file).suffix.lower() in (".jpg", ".jpeg"):
                for mirror in ("EXIF:ImageDescription", "IPTC:Caption-Abstract"):
                    exif_args.append(f"-{mirror}={desc}")
                    report.append(f"{mirror}: (mirrored)")
        if args.dry_run:
            print(f"hee-exif provenance --dry-run, would write to {file}:")
            for line in report:
                print(f"  {line}")
            continue
        r = run(exif_args + [file])
        if r.returncode != 0:
            print(f"hee-exif provenance: FAILED on {file}: {r.stderr.strip()}", file=sys.stderr)
            rc = 2
            continue
        print(f"hee-exif provenance: {file}")
        for line in report:
            print(f"  {line}")
    return rc


def gpg_sign_one(file, key, dry_run):
    """Real detached GPG signature (file.jpg.asc), same convention
    already used elsewhere in this repo (hee/cards/*.asc) -- not a
    custom EXIF-embedded crypto scheme. A detached .asc survives the
    metadata-stripping most photo hosts/re-exports do to EXIF; plain
    `gpg --verify` checks it.

    Real bug, found and fixed the same day: an earlier version of this
    function wrote a sha256 reference into the file's own EXIF
    *after* signing, as a "here's a checkable signature" pointer --
    but that write mutates the very bytes just signed, invalidating
    the signature (a self-referential-hash problem: the file's hash
    can't include a correct note about its own hash). Fix: don't
    touch the file at all here. The .asc sidecar sitting next to it
    IS the pointer -- same as the existing hee/cards/*.asc precedent,
    no embedded reference needed. Run this LAST regardless, after any
    `hee-exif sign` call, so nothing signs, then still gets modified
    by something else afterward."""
    asc_path = file + ".asc"
    gpg_cmd = ["gpg", "--batch", "--yes", "--detach-sign", "--armor", "--output", asc_path]
    if key:
        gpg_cmd += ["--local-user", key]
    gpg_cmd.append(file)

    if dry_run:
        print(f"hee-exif gpg-sign --dry-run: {file}")
        print(f"  would run: {' '.join(gpg_cmd)}")
        return True

    proc = run(gpg_cmd)
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        print(f"hee-exif: gpg sign failed for {file}:\n{proc.stderr}", file=sys.stderr)
        return False

    verify = run(["gpg", "--verify", asc_path, file])
    if verify.returncode != 0:
        print(f"hee-exif: wrote {asc_path} but self-check verify failed:\n{verify.stderr}", file=sys.stderr)
        return False

    print(f"hee-exif: wrote {asc_path}, verified good")
    print(f"verify yourself with: gpg --verify {asc_path} {file}")
    return True


def cmd_gpg_sign(args):
    ok = all([gpg_sign_one(f, args.key, args.dry_run) for f in args.files])
    if not ok:
        sys.exit(1)


def _replace_js_var(target_html, var_name, new_value_literal, kind):
    """Shared substitution core for regen-pubkey/embed-exif. Uses a
    function as re.sub's repl, not a string -- a real bug hit and
    fixed live (2026-08-26): a string repl gets its own backslash
    escapes re-processed by the re module (for \\g<name> group refs),
    which silently corrupts literal backslash sequences (e.g. "\\n" in
    an armored key, or inside a JSON string value) into something else
    entirely. A function's return value is inserted as-is."""
    with open(target_html, "r", encoding="utf-8") as f:
        content = f.read()
    pattern = re.compile(r"var " + re.escape(var_name) + r" = (?:\"[^\"]*\"|\{.*?\});", re.DOTALL)
    new_content, n = pattern.subn(lambda m: "var " + var_name + " = " + new_value_literal + ";", content)
    if n != 1:
        sys.exit(f"hee-exif {kind}: expected exactly 1 match for '{var_name}' in {target_html}, found {n}")
    with open(target_html, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
        f.write(new_content)


def _js_string_literal(s):
    return '"' + s.replace("\\", "\\\\").replace('"', '\\"').replace("\n", "\\n") + '"'


def cmd_regen_pubkey(args):
    url = f"https://github.com/{args.github_login}.gpg"
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=10) as r:
            armored = r.read().decode().rstrip("\n") + "\n"
    except Exception as e:
        sys.exit(f"hee-exif regen-pubkey: fetch failed for {url}: {e}")
    if "BEGIN PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK" not in armored:
        sys.exit(f"hee-exif regen-pubkey: fetched content for {args.github_login} doesn't look like a real key")
    _replace_js_var(args.target_html, args.var_name, _js_string_literal(armored), "regen-pubkey")
    print(f"hee-exif regen-pubkey: {args.var_name} <- {url} (refreshed)")


EXIF_LOCAL_ARTIFACT_FIELDS = {
    "SourceFile", "Directory", "FileAccessDate",
    "FileInodeChangeDate", "FileModifyDate", "FilePermissions",
}


def _is_blank(v):
    if v is None:
        return True
    if isinstance(v, str) and v.strip() == "":
        return True
    if isinstance(v, (list, dict)) and len(v) == 0:
        return True
    return False


def cmd_embed_exif(args):
    require_exiftool()
    exclude = set(EXIF_LOCAL_ARTIFACT_FIELDS)
    if args.exclude:
        exclude |= set(args.exclude.split(","))

    proc = run(["exiftool", "-json", args.photo_dir])
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        sys.exit(f"hee-exif embed-exif: exiftool failed: {proc.stderr}")
    # exiftool's JSON can contain raw control characters in text fields
    # (e.g. UserComment) that aren't valid strict JSON.
    data = json.loads(proc.stdout, strict=False)

    out = {}
    exts = tuple("." + e.strip().lower().lstrip(".") for e in (args.ext or "jpg,jpeg").split(","))
    for d in data:
        name = d.get("FileName", "")
        if not name.lower().endswith(exts):
            continue
        photo_id = name.rsplit(".", 1)[0]
        out[photo_id] = {k: v for k, v in d.items() if k not in exclude and not _is_blank(v)}

    if not out:
        sys.exit(f"hee-exif embed-exif: no {'/'.join(exts)} files found in {args.photo_dir}, refusing to embed nothing")

    embed = json.dumps(out, separators=(",", ":"), ensure_ascii=False)
    _replace_js_var(args.target_html, args.var_name, embed, "embed-exif")
    print(f"hee-exif embed-exif: embedded {len(out)} photo(s), {len(embed)} bytes, into {args.var_name}")


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="hee-exif")
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)

    r = sub.add_parser("read", help="dump all real EXIF/metadata for a file")
    r.add_argument("file")
    r.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")

    s = sub.add_parser("sign", help="write the real agent-instance-signature block + optional Artist/Copyright")
    s.add_argument("file")
    s.add_argument("--artist", default=None)
    s.add_argument("--copyright", default=None,
                    help=f"only set when real authorship/assignment is known -- not auto-applied. "
                         f"The real org legal name, if it ever legitimately applies, is: {TCOS_LEGAL_NAME!r}")
    s.add_argument("--force", action="store_true", help="overwrite an already-set Artist/Copyright")
    s.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")

    br = sub.add_parser("brand", help="write the org's default branding: credit/publisher, PEN identifier, license; Artist/Copyright defaulted unless given")
    br.add_argument("files", nargs="+")
    br.add_argument("--branding", default=None, help="branding card YAML (default: $HEE_BRANDING)")
    br.add_argument("--artist", default=None, help="whose work this is, when not ours")
    br.add_argument("--copyright", default=None, help="their notice, when the IP is someone else's")
    br.add_argument("--force", action="store_true", help="overwrite an existing real Artist/Copyright")
    br.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")

    es = sub.add_parser("embed-sig", help="put a GPG signature IN the file: sign its metadata-stripped form, store the armor in XMP-hee")
    es.add_argument("files", nargs="+")
    es.add_argument("--key", default=None, help="gpg --local-user selector; default signing key if omitted")
    es.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")

    vf = sub.add_parser("verify", help="verify the embedded signature (and a detached .asc if present); --pixels OURS compares decoded pixels; Nagios exit codes")
    vf.add_argument("files", nargs="+")
    vf.add_argument("--pixels", default=None, metavar="OURS", help="compare each file's decoded pixels, frame by frame, to this file or URL")
    vf.add_argument("--pixels-only", action="store_true", help="with --pixels: skip the signature checks (a platform copy has none)")

    pv = sub.add_parser("provenance", help="write how a GENERATED image was made: tool@commit, job, source (+sha256s), signed with the org rc_tag")
    pv.add_argument("files", nargs="+")
    pv.add_argument("--tool", required=True, help="generator name, e.g. meme-factory/faceoff")
    pv.add_argument("--commit", default=None, help="git commit of the generator")
    pv.add_argument("--job", default=None, help="job/recipe file that drove the render (sha256 recorded if it exists)")
    pv.add_argument("--source", default=None, help="input image (sha256 recorded if it exists)")
    pv.add_argument("--kv", action="append", default=None, metavar="K=V", help="extra provenance field, repeatable")
    pv.add_argument("--force", action="store_true", help="overwrite a non-provenance XMP-dc:Description")
    pv.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")

    g = sub.add_parser("gpg-sign", help="real detached GPG signature (file.asc) -- supports bulk, pass multiple files")
    g.add_argument("files", nargs="+")
    g.add_argument("--key", default=None, help="gpg --local-user selector (fingerprint or user-id); default gpg signing key if omitted")
    g.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")

    rp = sub.add_parser("regen-pubkey", help="front-load a GPG public key from github.com/<login>.gpg into a JS var in a target HTML file")
    rp.add_argument("target_html")
    rp.add_argument("var_name")
    rp.add_argument("github_login")

    ee = sub.add_parser("embed-exif", help="embed real, non-blank exiftool output for every photo in a dir into a JS var in a target HTML file")
    ee.add_argument("target_html")
    ee.add_argument("var_name")
    ee.add_argument("photo_dir")
    ee.add_argument("--exclude", default=None, help="comma-separated extra field names to exclude, added to the default local-artifact exclusion list")
    ee.add_argument("--ext", default=None, help="comma-separated extensions to embed (default: jpg,jpeg); e.g. jpg,png,gif for a media item that is not all photos")

    # Contextual help BEFORE argparse parses anything. argparse owns -h and
    # --help but not the bare `help` verb, and resolves either only after
    # parsing -- so an unrelated argument errors first and the help never
    # prints. Measured: 8 tools exited non-zero for --help for exactly this
    # reason. See library/py/hee_cli.
    if help_wanted(sys.argv[1:]):
        note_ignored(sys.argv[1:])
        ap.print_help()
        return 0

    args = ap.parse_args()
    # Subcommands return a Nagios code; it was being discarded, so verify
    # (and brand/provenance on a failed write) always exited 0 -- caught
    # 2026-09-05 proving embed-sig detects a tampered byte.
    rc = {
        "read": cmd_read, "sign": cmd_sign, "brand": cmd_brand, "provenance": cmd_provenance, "embed-sig": cmd_embed_sig, "verify": cmd_verify, "gpg-sign": cmd_gpg_sign,
        "regen-pubkey": cmd_regen_pubkey, "embed-exif": cmd_embed_exif,
    }[args.cmd](args)
    sys.exit(rc or 0)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
